    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update python-geolinks to 0.2.3 (0.2.1 and 0.2.2 crossed).

- 0.2.1 drops Python 2, adds type annotations and a click-based
  geolinks command line tool; registered here via libalternatives
- Add python-click: the RPM carried no click dependency at all, so
  both &quot;import geolinks&quot; and the new CLI failed on a fresh install
  (rpmlint W: python-missing-require). No floor invented - upstream
  requirements.txt is the bare name
- 0.2.2 renames LICENSE to LICENSE.md and fixes setup.py metadata
- 0.2.3 ships requirements.txt in the sdist, without which the
  0.2.2 sdist could not be built
- Source stays the tag archive: the PyPI sdist still ships no tests/
- %check now runs via %pytest; spec-cleaner clean, Group dropped,
  %setup -&gt; %autosetup

Local build openSUSE_Tumbleweed/aarch64 green, rpmlint 0 badness,
1 test passed per flavour (python313, python314).</comment>
    <requestid>1375669</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
